#: dist/wpsynchro.js:2
msgid "WP Synchro is a plugin that allows you to migrate/clone a WordPress site to another site, from one url to another url, either by migrating the entire site or selectively migrating parts of it."
msgstr ""

#: dist/wpsynchro.js:2
msgid "ONE SITE RUNS THE MIGRATION"
msgstr ""

#: dist/wpsynchro.js:2
msgid "It is important to know that migrations are run on one site and that site drives the migration to or from the other site. The browser watching the migration progress is the actual process that pokes the migration to continue and therefore the browser tab running the migration should not be closed before it is done."
msgstr ""

#: dist/wpsynchro.js:2
msgid "PUSH/PULL MIGRATION TERMINOLOGY"
msgstr ""

#: dist/wpsynchro.js:2
msgid "WP Synchro uses 'push' and 'pull' terminology to describe the direction of migrations. This can be a bit confusing when first meeting these terms."
msgstr ""

#: dist/wpsynchro.js:2
msgid "A 'push' migration is when you migrate away from the site you are on to the other site. Like 'pushing' data to the other site from the site we are running the migration on."
msgstr ""

#: dist/wpsynchro.js:2
msgid "A 'pull' migration is when you migrate from the other site to the site you are on. Like 'pulling' data to the site we are running the migration on."
msgstr ""

#: dist/wpsynchro.js:2
msgid "This also means that a migration can be run on either side of the migration. Site A pulling from Site B is the same as Site B pushing to Site A."
msgstr ""

